adjudication.rationale:
In PasskeysUsernamePasswordFormTest.reauthenticationOfUserWithoutPasskey(), the absence of the webauthn form is checked via a try/catch that catches a broad Exception:

```java
try {
  MatcherAssert.assertThat(driver.findElement(By.xpath("//form[@id='webauth']")), nullValue());
  fail("Not expected to have webauthn button");
} catch (Exception nsee) {
  // expected
}
```

Catching Exception will treat any WebDriver/runtime failure (timeouts, stale element, other driver errors) as the expected outcome, potentially letting the test pass even if the page is broken. This is inconsistent with the more precise element-absence check elsewhere in the diff (e.g., Assert.assertThrows(NoSuchElementException.class, ...)).
